    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "change-running-arpeggiation",
      "narrative": "Change-running (chord-arpeggiating) is the foundational device for the II-7 chord: the improviser arpeggiates the minor seventh chord to tune the ear to its structure, learn the progression, provide pickup notes, and clarify harmony. Coker states that a change-running phrase 'does not necessarily begin on the root of the chord, it may omit one or more chord members, and its direction can be ascending or descending or both' (p. 9). Practice across all 12 keys against exercise tracks that move in the cycle of fifths and chromatically.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
