    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "cesh-application",
      "narrative": "Although CESH's canonical setting is a minor chord of long duration, Coker extends its application to II-7 chords: 'the examples from recorded solos will reveal that improvisers will also use CESH on II-7 chords, V7 chords (the minor CESH will actually be built on the fifth of the V7, as in G [minor CESH] on a C7), or the II-V in combination' (p. 74). Students should practice CESH patterns in all keys against appropriate play-along tracks.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "coker-elements-jazz-language",
      "references": [
