    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "track-aa-half-diminished-substitution",
      "narrative": "In Track AA practice contexts, Coker specifies that the half-diminished chord substitutes for the minor seventh: 'the letters of the root sequence for Track AA is the same as that for Track Y (C, F, Bb, Eb, Ab, etc.)' but with half-diminished chords replacing minor sevenths (p. 32). This substitution rule applies specifically to the Track AA exercise context and introduces the minor II chord of the minor II-V progression.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
