    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "bebop-lick-tritone-substitution-extension",
      "narrative": "Coker extends the bebop lick's application beyond its basic dom7 context: 'Another interesting way to apply the bebop lick against dominant seventh chords is to use it as a means of playing tri-tone substitutions (or altered dominants), an element that will be taken up later in this book' (p. 44). This implies playing the bebop lick starting on the root of the tritone-substituted chord while the underlying chord is the original dominant seventh.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "coker-elements-jazz-language",
