    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "cesh-application-on-fifth",
      "narrative": "CESH is applicable over V7 chords by constructing the minor CESH on the fifth of the dominant: 'improvisers will also use CESH on... V7 chords (the minor CESH will actually be built on the fifth of the V7, as in G [minor CESH] on a C7)' (p. 74). This extends CESH beyond its canonical minor-chord-of-long-duration context into the II-V motion.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
      "source_work_id": "coker-elements-jazz-language",
