    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "harmonic-generalization-tonic-major",
      "narrative": "The V7 chord is covered by the tonic major scale under harmonic generalization: 'A G7 chord uses, among other possibilities, a G mixolydian scale, which again, is a C major scale beginning on G. Hence a progression of D-7, G7, C [major] could be realized by simply playing a C major scale or a pattern on that scale' (p. 45). The C pentatonic also covers C7 and G7sus with no collision tones.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
