    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "sharp-ii-diminished-seventh-substitute",
      "narrative": "The #II dim7 chord may be used to substitute for V7: 'Like the back door progression, the #II dim7 is often used to precede the I chord (or III-7, a substitute for I) in a given progression, leading to the improvised use of #II dim7 in place of a given V7 chord' (p. 82). Coker explains this works because 'the listener's ear hears the given precedents for the event, instead of the conflict with the V7.'",
