    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "three-flat-nine-practice-contexts",
      "narrative": "Coker prescribes specific harmonic contexts for practicing the 3-b9 device against dom7: 'The harmonic settings that are most appropriate are dominant seventh chords, dominant seventh chords moving around the cycle of fifths, II-7 to V7 cells moving downward in whole steps, and II-7 to V7 (alt.) moving downward in whole steps' (p. 31). These four practice contexts systematically cover the most common real-tune dominant-seventh settings.",
