    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "cry-me-a-river-lick-starting-point",
      "narrative": "The Cry Me A River lick starts on the 13th of a dominant seventh chord: the lick 'starts on the: ninth of the -7 chord / thirteenth of the 7 chord / fourth of the [major] chord / augmented ninth of the 7 (+5, +9) chord / major seventh of the [+5 major] chord' (p. 73). Because the lick accommodates five chord types without alteration, its application to dom7 (starting on the 13th) is one of its highest-frequency uses.",
      "source_principle_ids": [],
