    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7alt",
      "function_role": "altered-dominant-definition",
      "narrative": "Coker defines the altered dominant precisely: 'The altered dominant is a dominant seventh chord which contains, in its complete realization, an augmented fifth (+5), a flatted ninth (b9), an augmented ninth (+9), and an augmented eleventh (+11, or +4). Tri-tone substitutions and altered dominants are nearly identical, as shown below' (p. 82). The structural near-identity to the tritone substitute is the theoretical basis for their interchangeability in improvisation.",
