      "function_role": "cry-me-a-river-lick-starting-point",
      "narrative": "The Cry Me A River lick starts on the +9 of the altered dominant: the lick starts on the 'augmented ninth of the 7 (+5, +9) chord' (p. 73). Since the lick accommodates five chord types without alteration, practitioners should identify and memorize the +9 starting tone for each key to deploy the lick fluently over altered dominant chords. The Gone But Not Forgotten lick is prescribed for the same five chord contexts.",
