      "narrative": "The C pentatonic scale covers the Gb7 altered dominant without collision tones: 'a C pentatonic scale (C, D, E, G, A) will fit... a Gb7 (+5, b9) with not one colliding [pitch]' (p. 45). This is the most harmonically distant of the ten chord types covered by a single pentatonic and demonstrates the device's particular value for handling tritone-substituted altered dominants.",
